108-sional simple Lie algebra, cf. Theorem 4.3. Theorem 4.3 is a generalization of
109-[17, Theorem 8.4]. For a certain subclass of the Seifert manifolds, containing all
110-the Seifert fibered integral homology spheres, we simplify the expression for the
111-invariants considerable, cf. Theorem 4.8. This result is a generalization of [33,
112-Formula (4.2)]. Secondly, we analyse more carefully the invariants τrg(X) for X
113:any lens space. Theorem 5.1 gives the result for any lens space and any of the
114-invariants τrg . Proposition 5.2 gives more compact expressions for τrg(L(p, q))
115:in case r and p are coprime. A main corollary of Theorem 5.1, Corollary 5.5,
116-is a determination of the large r asymptotics of the quantum g–invariants of
117-the lens spaces. The result is in agreement with the AEC, and leads together
118-with the AEC to a Conjecture 5.6 for the Chern–Simons invariants of the flat G
119-connections on any lens space, G being an arbitrary simply connected, compact
